# Reachability coverage baseline (CC-22 ratcheting list).
#
# Each line is the name of a `WorkflowEngine` impl that has NO matching
# `tests/reachability/<snake_case>.rs` file. Today's gap was 28 engines
# with tests vs 14 covered (audit P-11/R-4, 2026-05-08); the gate can
# only ratchet down, never up. New `WorkflowEngine` impls must ship
# with a test (rejected if the engine name is missing from the
# baseline AND no test file exists). When a test for a baseline entry
# lands, REMOVE that entry — the gate fails if a baseline entry has a
# corresponding test, forcing shrinkage to track real coverage.
#
# Mapping rule: engine name has the trailing `Engine` stripped, then
# CamelCase boundaries become underscores, then lower-cased.
# `ContactListEngine` → `contact_list.rs`. Edge cases (consecutive
# capitals, etc.) — when they appear, prefer renaming the engine over
# special-casing the gate.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
# AppEngine is the composition root: current_screen/handle_action delegate to
# the per-sub-state engines (each now has its own reachability test above). A
# standalone test would need a full Vauchi instance and re-walk those same
# screens, so it is intentionally retained here rather than ratcheted out.
AppEngine

